{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And for a frontlet.</b> Tefillin; and because they are four compartments they are called <b>טטפת</b> — 'טט' in Coptic is two, 'פת' in African is two (Sanhedrin 4). And Menachem grouped it with ״וְהַטֵּף אֶל דָּרוֹם״ (Ezekiel 21), ״אַל תַּטִּיפוּ״ (Micah 2) — a term of speech, like 'and for a remembrance': whoever sees them bound between the eyes will remember the miracle and speak of it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:57.948846992Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}